# Project Startup

Before planning, editing, or running project commands, restore context from these
(`AGENTS.md` is already in context — `CLAUDE.md` imports it, or it was read as the rule source — so do not re-read it):

- `docs/arch/code-map.md` — module layout, entry points, test locations.
- `AGENTS.md` "Current Actions and Known Gaps" — action items and known gaps; enough to plan the next step.
- `docs/PROJECT_STATUS.md` — only when you need the current milestone or verification-baseline numbers.

Do NOT read `初步入库评测指标.md` at startup — it is 3,000+ lines. It is the single authoritative source
for every metric caliber; read only the relevant section when actually working on a metric. Its head
carries a wide-table inclusion index, and its tail appendix holds the wide-table cell contract, the
cancelled/deferred metric register, the open business-confirmation items, and the full-sample baseline.

For operational tasks (log salvage, full wide-table recompute, report generation),
read the matching manual under `docs/runbooks/` before running scripts.

Always inspect `git status` before editing and preserve unrelated user changes.
Never implement a concrete metric until its formula, field mapping, boundary behavior,
and worked example have been shown to the user and explicitly approved.

After a verified batch, update `docs/PROJECT_STATUS.md` when the current milestone,
next action, known blockers, or verification baseline changed.
